Medicine degree from Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine. Following her veterinary degree, Dr. McMillan completed a yearlong small animal rotating internship at Michigan Veterinary Specialists. She furthered her training by completing a residency in veterinary oncology at Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine, while also obtaining her Master of Science degree in comparative and veterinary oncology.\nDr. McMillan has a profound interest in all aspects of veterinary oncology, with a special focus on bladder cancer, electrochemotherapy, lymphoma, and novel cancer treatments. She has published several articles, including studies on bladder cancer in Journal of the American Veterinary Medical Association, urethral stenting for bladder tumors in Journal of the American Veterinary Medical Association, histiocytic sarcoma in Veterinary and Comparative Oncology, malignant melanoma in Veterinary and Comparative Oncology and The Canadian Veterinary Journal, and coauthored a book chapter on bladder cancer in the book Small Animal Oncology. One of her favorite aspects of practicing veterinary oncology is helping families understand their options so they can choose the best treatment path for their beloved pets. She takes great pleasure in providing families with the valuable extra time they can have with their companions.\nOutside of her professional responsibilities, Dr. Sarah McMillan enjoys traveling, scuba diving, and spending time with her husband and cherished cats.\nEducation & Training\nBachelor of Science:\nPurdue University\nDoctor of Veterinary Medicine:\nPurdue University College of Veterinary Medicine\nInternship (Rotating Small Animal Medicine and Surgery):\nMichigan Veterinary Specialists\nMaster of Science:\nPurdue University\nResidency (Medical Oncology):\nPurdue University College of Veterinary Medicine\nSpecializations\nBoard Certification:\nDiplomate of the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (Oncology)\nAssociations\nAmerican Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA)\nAmerican College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM)\nVeterinary Cancer Society (VCS)\nAwards & Recognition\nBladder cancer in Journal of the American Veterinary Medical Association\nUrethral stenting for bladder tumors in Journal of the American Veterinary Medical Association\nHistiocytic sarcoma in Veterinary and Comparative Oncology\nMalignant melanoma in Veterinary and Comparative Oncology\nMalignant melanoma in The Canadian Veterinary Journal\nCoauthored a book chapter on bladder cancer in the book Small Animal Oncology\nSpecialties\nMedical Oncology\nServicing Locations\nMedVet Northern Virginia\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
